# Form components

## Default: Radix UI

Use **Radix UI** (`radix-ui` / `@radix-ui/*`) for general forms and overlays:

- Text, Select, Checkbox, Switch, Radio, Slider
- Dialog, Alert Dialog, Popover, Dropdown Menu, Context Menu, Tabs
- Native `input` / `textarea` only when wrapped by Radix Form (or project ChatSelect / ConfirmModal patterns)

Do **not** use native `type="date"`, `type="datetime-local"`, or `type="time"` for new UI.

## Dates & times: React Aria Components

Use **`react-aria-components`** + **`@internationalized/date`** for:

- date
- date range
- datetime
- datetime range
- time (when a dedicated picker is needed)

Prefer existing wrappers when present (e.g. `ChatDatePicker`, `ChatDateTimePicker`). Compose `DatePicker` / `DateRangePicker` / `DateField` / `TimeField` with `Calendar` / `RangeCalendar` rather than browser date inputs.

```jsx
// ❌ BAD
<input type="date" value={date} onChange={...} />
<input type="datetime-local" value={from} onChange={...} />

// ✅ GOOD
import { parseDate, parseDateTime } from '@internationalized/date';
import { DatePicker, DateRangePicker } from 'react-aria-components';
// or project wrappers: ChatDatePicker, ChatDateTimePicker
```

Wire values through `@internationalized/date` (`CalendarDate`, `CalendarDateTime`, ranges) and convert at the boundary if storage/API still needs ISO / `YYYY-MM-DD` / `datetime-local` strings.
